### 3. Graph Node Hierarchy & Branching Taxonomy

#### 3.1 Main Root Node: `STORED SECURITY INTELLIGENCE`
* **Visual Presentation:** Positioned on the far left ($X \approx 80\text{px}$). Features a dark planetary aura with a radiant glowing core orb surrounded by particle iris rings (`animate-pulse-glow`).
* **Root Telemetry Badges:**
  * `Total Stored Records: 1,428`
  * `Monitored Accounts: 18`
  * `Observed IPs: 24`
  * `Archived Incidents: 16`
  * `Last Database Archive: 3 mins ago`

#### 3.2 Generation 1: Primary Category Nodes
All ten branches connect to the root via smooth, cubic SVG Bezier curves (`M x1 y1 C cx1 y1, cx2 y2, x2 y2`):
1. **`👥 USER RECORDS`** (18 Historical Accounts)
2. **`🔑 LOGIN HISTORY`** (842 Authentication Records)
3. **`🚨 SECURITY EVENTS`** (1,240 Normalized Security Events)
4. **`🔐 PASSWORD & ACCOUNT HISTORY`** (32 Credential Changes)
5. **`💻 DEVICE HISTORY`** (14 Known Hardware Assets)
6. **`🌐 IP ADDRESS HISTORY`** (24 Observed IP Subnets)
7. **`⚠️ ALERT & INCIDENT ARCHIVE`** (16 Triaged Incidents)
8. **`⏱️ SESSION HISTORY`** (128 OAuth & JWT Sessions)
9. **`🔍 DETECTION EVIDENCE`** (9 Correlation Cases)
10. **`📋 AUDIT HISTORY`** (48 Admin Operation Logs)

#### 3.3 Generation 2: Category to Record Expansion
When a user clicks any category node, it receives an illuminated active border (`ring-1 ring-amber-400` or `ring-cyan-400`), and sprouts an elegant **radial fan-out array of child nodes** to the right:
* **When `USER RECORDS` is active:** Fans out 6–10 monitored user nodes (`Sarah Chen`, `Marcus Vance`, `Elena Rostova`, `David Kim`, etc.), each tagged with role and risk badges (`HIGH RISK 88`, `CRITICAL 94`).
* **When `SECURITY EVENTS` is active:** Fans out normalized event categories (`Login Failure`, `Impossible Travel`, `MFA Bombing`, `Tor Reset`, `Password Changed`).
* **When `ALERT & INCIDENT ARCHIVE` is active:** Fans out categorized severity groups (`Critical Alerts`, `High-Risk Alerts`, `Investigated Incidents`, `Resolved Incidents`).

#### 3.4 Generation 3: Record to Evidence & Contextual Entity Expansion
Selecting an individual entity node expands the next generation of child nodes:
* Expanding `User 001 (Sarah Chen)` produces:
  * `[Profile]` $\rightarrow$ Email, Role, Department, MFA Status.
  * `[Login Events]` $\rightarrow$ Date groups (October 2026, September 2026) $\rightarrow$ Specific Event IDs.
  * `[Observed Devices]` $\rightarrow$ `MacBookPro-M3-Corp (Chrome)`, `iPhone-15-Corp`.
  * `[Associated IPs]` $\rightarrow$ `198.51.100.44 (US)`, `185.220.101.5 (Tor Exit)`.
  * `[Incident History]` $\rightarrow$ `INC-8821 Impossible Travel Violation`.

---

### 4. Right-Side Stored Intelligence Inspector (~30% Width)

The inspector is a floating glass card that reacts dynamically to node selection:

#### 4.1 Header & Overview
* Entity category icon (Shield, User, Laptop, Globe, or Alert).
* Entity title & role (e.g. `Sarah Chen — Lead Cloud Architect`).
* Status pill: `[ACTIVE]` with timestamp: `The last update was archived on 01 Oct 2026`.
* Primary action button: `[ Explore details > ]` (White or dark rounded pill).

#### 4.2 Risk Contribution Rate & Sparkline Histogram
* Big percentage: **`45%`** (Risk Contribution Rate) with change indicator **`-4% last month`**.
* **Mini Vertical Bar Histogram Sparkline:** 24 animated vertical bars displaying density/velocity over time, with the anomalous peak highlighted in gold/amber.

#### 4.3 2x2 Telemetry Metric Grid
* `[✓ 12 Correlated Alerts & Findings]`
* `[📄 2 Associated Devices]`
* `[🌐 18 Observed IP Addresses]`
* `[✓ 12 Active / Historical Sessions]`

#### 4.4 AI Forensic Copilot Analysis Card
* Icon: `RI Analysis / AI Forensic Copilot`.
* Title: `Historical Anomaly Assessment`.
* Synthesis text: *"User exhibit 4.2x velocity spike between consecutive logins. 7 failed login attempts preceded immediate password reset request from Tor Exit Node 185.220.101.5."*

#### 4.5 Interactive Copilot Prompt & Quick Filters
* Rounded input field: `"Ask a question about this historical node..."` with arrow button.
* Filter tags beneath input: `[+ My agent]`, `[⏱️ +3]`, `[AI Synthesis]`.

---

### 5. Interaction & Animation Requirements
1. **Smooth Bezier Drawing:** Lines are rendered using `<path d="M... C...">` with dynamic curvature based on distance.
2. **Animated Traveling Packets:** Small glowing SVG circles traverse along active paths (`animateMotion`) to visualize data linkage.
3. **Branch Collapse & Expansion:** Expanding a branch smoothly slides child nodes in with opacity and translate transitions.
4. **Canvas Controls:** Pan, zoom (`+` / `-`), auto-fit view, and reset canvas.

---

### 6. Technical Implementation Blueprint
* **Component Structure:**
  * `src/components/analyzer/AnalyzerCanvas.tsx`: Interactive SVG + HTML node canvas.
  * `src/components/analyzer/RootNode.tsx`: Planetary aura root node.
  * `src/components/analyzer/CategoryNode.tsx`: First-generation category pills.
  * `src/components/analyzer/FanOutNode.tsx`: Second-generation child entity pills.
  * `src/components/analyzer/SubBranchNode.tsx`: Third-generation evidence nodes.
  * `src/components/analyzer/InspectorPanel.tsx`: Fixed 30% right-side inspection drawer with histogram.
  * `src/components/analyzer/AnalyzerTopBar.tsx`: Graph tools (zoom, pan, search, filter).
* **Navigation Integration:**
  * Top navigation tab switcher:
    * **`📊 Living Dashboard`** (Our executive SOC interface).
    * **`🕸️ Stored Intelligence Graph (Analyzer)`** (This new OSINT graph investigation tab).

